  "body": "Although technically this could lead to exfiltration, that is already possible through `<iframe>`. So the protection the standard has is largely theoretical, moot in practice, and not implemented in browsers.\n\nSince request's origin is only reset during redirects for CORS, fixing this shouldn't be too tricky. Need to decide whether to simply set response tainting to basic or move to a different concept altogether.\n",
